@startuml preflight
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Preflight and ticket reconciliation

state "Refresh task inputs\nRe-fetch Jira ticket if linked; design version,\ntarget branch/commit, dependencies" as Refresh
state "Resolve authoritative project guidance\nLocate configured design and instructions\nCheck authority and consistency with task intent" as Guidance
state "Assess task relevance\nMap each acceptance criterion\nto current code and evidence" as Assess
state Decision <<choice>>
state "Correct stale ticket\nRecord old/new facts and rationale\nPreserve original intent" as Correct
state "Mark Jira ticket unneeded\nRecord explanation + evidence\nClose and verify resolution" as Close
state "Close prompt-only task without code\nRecord explanation + evidence\nVerify internal task status" as PromptClose
state "Verify prerequisites\nConfirm outcome exists in target code" as Dependency
state "Reconcile saved branch\nCheck prior handoff against current base\nRecord conflicts as new repair context" as Restore
state "Freeze task specification\nScope, acceptance criteria, context,\nconfiguration and policy versions" as Spec
state "Reconcile pending PR/response or delivery intent\nBind human reply to actor, task, PR + head\nCompare current spec, senior review, checks and remote code" as ResumeCheck
state "Ready for implementation" as Ready <<success>>
state "Resume delivery/recovery\nPrior PR or direct-push intent identified" as ResumePublication <<success>>
state "Jira ticket closed as unneeded\nNo implementation needed" as NotNeeded <<success>>
state "Prompt task closed as unneeded\nNo implementation needed" as PromptNotNeeded <<success>>
state "Clarification required\nDo not rewrite intent or guess" as Clarify <<attention>>
state "Dependency blocked\nCreate/link prerequisite and hand off" as ScopeBlock <<blocked>>

[*] --> Refresh
Refresh --> Guidance : resolved repository + current inputs captured
Guidance --> Assess : guidance identified; authority/intent clear
Guidance --> Clarify : required design missing or inaccessible\n/ request project guidance; do not guess
Guidance --> Clarify : design contradicts task; intended authority unclear\n/ record conflict and request resolution
Assess --> Decision : assessment recorded
Decision --> Correct : [incorrect/stale; same intended task]
Correct --> Refresh : update confirmed / reassess
Correct --> Refresh : revision conflict / reread; bounded retries
Decision --> Close : [Jira-backed; unnecessary or already satisfied;\nno pending delivery] and evidence sufficient
Decision --> PromptClose : [prompt-only; unnecessary or already satisfied;\nno pending delivery] and evidence sufficient
Decision --> Dependency : [human response or delivery recovery pending;\ncurrent task/design/ticket intent reconciled]\n/ verify prerequisites and saved branch before resumption
Close --> NotNeeded : explanation + resolution confirmed
PromptClose --> PromptNotNeeded : explanation + task status confirmed
Close --> Refresh : relevant inputs changed / reassess
Decision --> Clarify : [uncertain or conflicting]
Decision --> Dependency : [valid and still needed]
Decision --> ScopeBlock : [necessary prerequisite outside scope]
Dependency --> ScopeBlock : unresolved / not available in code
Dependency --> Restore : satisfied; previous work exists
Dependency --> Spec : satisfied; no previous work
Restore --> Spec : saved work assessed; repair needs recorded
Restore --> Clarify : unsafe or ambiguous reconciliation
Spec --> Ready : [new work; no pending delivery]\npolicy + freshness checks pass
Spec --> ResumeCheck : [pending human response or delivery recovery]\ncurrent spec + policy frozen
Spec --> Refresh : source revisions materially changed
ResumeCheck --> ResumePublication : [approved response or delivery recovery;\ncurrent spec, PR/head, senior approval + checks match]\nor target publication verified and status pending
ResumeCheck --> Ready : [in-scope feedback or stale approval/checks]\n/ preserve response and old work as repair context;
ResumeCheck --> ScopeBlock : confirmed necessary work outside scope
ResumeCheck --> Clarify : ambiguous actor, PR, scope, review binding\nor contradictory fresh inputs
ResumeCheck --> Refresh : ticket/design/target changed during check\n/ reassess before any merge or repair
Ready --> [*] : return ready
ResumePublication --> [*] : return publication_resume
NotNeeded --> [*] : return no_work
PromptNotNeeded --> [*] : return no_work
Clarify --> [*] : return attention
ScopeBlock --> [*] : return scope_blocked

note right of Assess
  Read the target project's design, not only
  Slop Machine's design or an agent summary.
  Failure to reproduce is not proof of no work.
  Published code awaiting completion is not an unnecessary ticket.
  Preflight role and closure review threshold: TBD.
end note
note left of Guidance
  A demonstrably stale ticket with unchanged intent can
  still reach Correct after assessment. Conflicting intent
  cannot be silently resolved by rewriting requirements.
  A no-design exception policy has not been selected.
end note
note right of ResumeCheck
  New-run preflight precedes every human response and recovery action.
  Corrections and conflicting intent take priority over resumption.
  A response requesting changes enters implementation with the current
  spec and feedback; it needs new checks, senior review and human review.
  A stale old approval never authorizes merge of a new PR head/spec.
end note
note right of Correct
  Corrections cannot enlarge the task's scope.
  New required work goes to a prerequisite ticket.
  Mutations use policy checks and reconciliation;
  unconfirmed updates never count as success.
end note
note bottom of Spec
  Fresh implementation/reviewer sessions are created lazily after readiness.
  The specification and evidence survive replacement of agent sessions.
  Operational failures follow operation-guardrails.puml; exhausted recovery returns attention.
end note
@enduml
